############ HOW TO READ IT ############
  1. Look at arm=none first. If it is clean and host/device are not, the
     staging change is implicated. If it fails too, the connector was
     already broken on this matrix and this experiment is blocked.
  2. exit=3 means the harness caught the CUDA fault itself and printed
     the exact dataset/compressor pair on a [FATAL] line. Start there.
  3. A cudaMalloc 'illegal memory access' is NOT an allocation failure.
     It is a sticky context error from an earlier kernel. The harness now
     detects that and stops instead of blaming the next dataset.
  4. Any [FAIL] fidelity line invalidates that pair's timings regardless
     of exit status.

